WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.115 --> 00:00:13.935
us out!"

2
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:15.695
Zann pounded on the door.

3
00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:20.017
"You can't hold us prisoner—we didn't do anything wrong!"

4
00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:23.618
Zing sensed the frustration in his master's voice.

5
00:00:24.338 --> 00:00:27.298
Leaping forward, the dragon tried to burn a hole in the door.

6
00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:30.579
Suddenly—zap! Zing disappeared!

7
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.700
"No!" Darb cried.

8
00:00:33.124 --> 00:00:34.084
"What happened to Zing?"

9
00:00:34.104 --> 00:00:37.525
"It's okay," Yog called from out in the hallway.

10
00:00:37.545 --> 00:00:38.786
"I'll look after him."

11
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:40.846
"Let us out!"

12
00:00:41.266 --> 00:00:41.847
Gliss cried.

13
00:00:42.687 --> 00:00:45.668
The only answer was the sound of footsteps hurrying away.

14
00:00:46.548 --> 00:00:47.528
Perda kicked the door.

15
00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:49.149
"This is horrible!"

16
00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.129
she exclaimed.

17
00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:51.509
"I know."

18
00:00:52.069 --> 00:00:53.250
Zann clenched his fists.

19
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.211
"I say we test that Shield spell.

20
00:00:57.031 --> 00:01:00.892
I bet if we all focus our energy together, we can beat the spell."

21
00:01:02.168 --> 00:01:04.070
"No!" Gliss looked alarmed.

22
00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.472
"If we use magic, Morb will know exactly where we are!

23
00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:09.974
He got into the palace before."

24
00:01:10.774 --> 00:01:11.475
Darb nodded.

25
00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:16.619
"Besides, that Shield spell was probably installed by skilled Magic Masters."

26
00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:20.041
"And we're just a bunch of kids," Perda added.

27
00:01:20.061 --> 00:01:22.383
"It's not worth the risk."

28
00:01:23.604 --> 00:01:27.566
Zann frowned, ready to argue, but he realized his friends were right.

29
00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.628
"Okay," he said.

30
00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.623
"But zapping can't be the only way to get out of a room.

31
00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:36.066
Let's see if we can figure out another way to escape."

32
00:01:36.086 --> 00:01:37.888
"What's the point?"

33
00:01:38.328 --> 00:01:38.929
Gliss sighed.

34
00:01:38.949 --> 00:01:42.312
"Like Perda said, we're just a bunch of kids.

35
00:01:43.132 --> 00:01:46.075
We can't possibly beat someone as powerful as Morb."

36
00:01:46.095 --> 00:01:50.239
"We can't do anything while we're trapped in here," Zann said.

37
00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:55.244
"If the people at the palace don't want to help us, we need to find someone who will.

38
00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:03.026
I still remember where a few of Boz's powerful Magic Master friends live, including his best friend, Teplo.

39
00:02:03.947 --> 00:02:07.430
Maybe some of them have managed to avoid being caught by the trolls.

40
00:02:08.251 --> 00:02:12.915
If we find Boz's friends and tell them what we've learned, they might know what to do."

41
00:02:14.116 --> 00:02:15.016
Perda looked hopeful.

42
00:02:15.036 --> 00:02:17.779
"That sounds like a good plan," she said.

43
00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:21.242
"It's too bad that Slib took Boz's diary though.

44
00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:22.122
We might need it."

45
00:02:22.863 --> 00:02:23.644
Zann shrugged.

46
00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.021
"I remember most of what was in there.

47
00:02:26.822 --> 00:02:27.162
Come on.

48
00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:28.843
Let's figure out how to escape."

49
00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:32.325
The kids spent the next few minutes searching for an exit.

50
00:02:33.025 --> 00:02:34.686
First they tested the main door.

51
00:02:35.406 --> 00:02:38.248
But it was thick, solid wood, and the lock was strong.

52
00:02:39.248 --> 00:02:43.150
There were only two other doors in the room, and they just led to the bedrooms.

53
00:02:43.991 --> 00:02:48.273
The windows behind the elegant curtains were crisscrossed with strong iron bars.

54
00:02:49.073 --> 00:02:51.555
And the air vents were too small to offer escape.

55
00:02:51.575 --> 00:02:54.781
"It's no use," Perda said at last.

56
00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:55.922
"We're trapped."

57
00:02:56.722 --> 00:02:58.704
Gliss collapsed onto a velvet sofa.

58
00:02:58.724 --> 00:03:01.386
"At least we're trapped in a nice place.

59
00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:05.690
Probably a lot nicer than wherever Morb is keeping his prisoners."

60
00:03:08.372 --> 00:03:13.316
Morb waved a hand to light another torch on the wall of the large, gloomy underground room.

61
00:03:14.097 --> 00:03:17.500
It was dark, and the ancient texts were difficult to read.

62
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.604
He leaned closer to the dusty old book, studying the scrawled lines on the page.

63
00:03:23.368 --> 00:03:30.312
Then he glanced across the room at his newest contraption: a menacing creation built of bones, wire, and

64
00:03:30.372 --> 00:03:31.513
other various objects.

65
00:03:32.353 --> 00:03:35.935
It hadn't been easy to get some of those things, even with his new power.

66
00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.197
But the magical device was almost ready.

67
00:03:39.918 --> 00:03:46.541
A few more items, a touch of magical energy, and all of Magica would be forced to bow

68
00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:47.162
before him.

69
00:03:47.942 --> 00:03:49.343
Hearing footsteps, he turned.

70
00:03:49.643 --> 00:03:50.864
The old woman had arrived.

71
00:03:51.572 --> 00:03:55.875
Morb's amber eyes went immediately to the large, lumpy sack she was holding.

72
00:03:55.895 --> 00:03:57.196
"You're late.

73
00:03:58.757 --> 00:04:01.559
Are those the paralyzer pythons from Fardark?"

74
00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.782
"Yes." She lifted the writhing, hissing sack.

75
00:04:05.802 --> 00:04:09.705
"Acquiring them involved great trouble and risk."

76
00:04:09.725 --> 00:04:14.208
"Give them to me," he ordered, striding forward and grabbing the sack.

77
00:04:14.909 --> 00:04:15.849
She stared at him.

78
00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:18.671
"What need do you have for such creatures?"

79
00:04:19.131 --> 00:04:19.612
she asked.

80
00:04:20.408 --> 00:04:23.129
"Their magic is unpredictable and can be deadly."

81
00:04:23.149 --> 00:04:25.450
"Don't question me."

82
00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.291
Morb tossed the sack into a corner.

83
00:04:28.972 --> 00:04:32.253
He would add the pythons to his contraption after the woman left.

84
00:04:32.913 --> 00:04:37.915
He didn't want anyone else to know how the thing was constructed, least of all an old busybody

85
00:04:37.955 --> 00:04:38.436
like her.

86
00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:40.136
She was still frowning.

87
00:04:40.156 --> 00:04:42.977
"I've done all you asked of me," she said.

88
00:04:42.997 --> 00:04:46.019
"My debt to you is repaid twice over.

89
00:04:46.739 --> 00:04:48.880
This will be the last time I help you."

90
00:04:49.804 --> 00:04:52.126
"Not so fast," Morb said.

91
00:04:52.146 --> 00:04:55.829
"I still need a few things that only you can get."

92
00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.792
Glaring at him, she stretched to her full height.

93
00:04:59.812 --> 00:05:02.234
"And if I refuse?"

94
00:05:03.174 --> 00:05:03.995
Morb shrugged.

95
00:05:04.015 --> 00:05:09.399
"If you refuse, I will be forced to tell everyone your unpleasant secrets."

96
00:05:09.799 --> 00:05:10.480
He smirked.

97
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:16.700
"Besides, if you wish to remain in Magica, you shouldn't anger me, Wyssa.

98
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.483
My power grows with every passing day."

99
00:05:20.283 --> 00:05:23.266
To demonstrate, he touched his fingers lightly together.

100
00:05:24.047 --> 00:05:29.712
Sparks flew everywhere from the slight friction, bouncing off the walls and turning the room into a fireworks

101
00:05:29.732 --> 00:05:34.536
display. The old woman ducked as a spark lit her skirt on fire.

102
00:05:35.356 --> 00:05:38.279
Morb smiled as he felt energy surge through him.

103
00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.724
Capturing Boz and some of the other Magic Masters had given him a taste of true power.

104
00:05:44.512 --> 00:05:47.815
The king and queen had increased his strength even more.

105
00:05:47.835 --> 00:05:50.557
"Impressive display, Morb."

106
00:05:51.277 --> 00:05:54.680
The old woman calmly touched the flames on her dress to put them out.

107
00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:59.904
"But don't forget that the power you steal through the leeches is temporary."

108
00:06:01.305 --> 00:06:03.746
Morb's eyes shifted toward his contraption.

109
00:06:04.487 --> 00:06:07.289
True, the leeches couldn't keep him strong forever.

110
00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:11.132
But soon he wouldn't need their temporary magic anymore.

111
00:06:11.848 --> 00:06:14.731
Suddenly he couldn't wait to get back to work on his project.

112
00:06:15.451 --> 00:06:18.234
It was time to finish it and seize his destiny.

113
00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:22.117
The trolls would just have to manage without him for the next day or two.

114
00:06:22.137 --> 00:06:26.341
"It is time for you to go, old woman," he told Wyssa.

115
00:06:26.361 --> 00:06:28.343
"I have much to do."
